        <div class="tab-content" id="tab-settings" data-main="settings" data-sub="general">
            <h3>Scheduled scanning &amp; collection</h3>
            <div class="info">
                Values saved here go into <code>scanner-settings.json</code> inside the plugin's data folder and
                <strong>override the same keys in the server's config.json</strong> - immediately and without a
                restart. config.json is never written by the plugin and remains the fallback
                ("from config.json" / "built-in default"). Use a field's <em>revert</em> option or the
                <em>Reset all</em> button to hand control back to config.json. The configuration for vulnerability
                data (NVD, CPE table) and for license keys lives under their own navigation items.
            </div>
            <div class="setgrid">
                <label for="setInterval">Scan interval (hours)</label>
                <div><input type="text" id="setInterval" class="num">
                    <select id="setIntervalSrc" class="srcsel"></select>
                    <div class="hint">Measured from the end of the last scan; restart-proof. 24 = daily, 168 = weekly, 720 = monthly, 0 = scheduled scans off.</div></div>

                <label for="setAnyAge">Suppress version-less CVEs older than (years)</label>
                <div><input type="text" id="setAnyAge" class="num">
                    <select id="setAnyAgeSrc" class="srcsel"></select>
                    <div class="hint">"any version" CPE matches older than N years are hidden; 0 = never.</div></div>

                <label for="setCollectInterval">Collect inventory every (minutes)</label>
                <div><input type="text" id="setCollectInterval" class="num">
                    <select id="setCollectIntervalSrc" class="srcsel"></select>
                    <div class="hint">1440 = daily, 0 = periodic collection off (offline devices keep their last list).</div></div>

                <label for="setCollectOnConnect">Collect when an agent connects</label>
                <div><input type="checkbox" id="setCollectOnConnect">
                    <div class="hint">Staggered randomly (5s to 5min) so reconnecting fleets do not cause a load spike.</div></div>

                <label for="setAutoMatch">Auto-map unknown software names to CPE products</label>
                <div><input type="checkbox" id="setAutoMatch">
                    <div class="hint">Programs without a table entry are matched against the CPE product names that actually exist in the
                    downloaded NVD data (name cleaned, publisher as vendor evidence, versions always re-checked). Offline, no configuration
                    needed; switch off to use only the curated + custom tables.</div></div>

                <label for="setDistroManaged">Linux distribution packages: trust the distribution while the OS is supported</label>
                <div><input type="checkbox" id="setDistroManaged">
                    <div class="hint">Packages installed from the distribution (dpkg/rpm/apk/pacman, maintained by Ubuntu/Debian/Red Hat/...)
                    get their security fixes as backports into the SAME upstream version, so an NVD version check only produces false
                    alarms. With this on they are reported as "patched by the distribution" while the OS release is supported, and as
                    end-of-life (finding OS-EOL) once it is not. Third-party repositories (Docker, NVIDIA, ...) are still checked normally.</div></div>

                <label for="setOsLifecycleEnabled">Fetch OS support dates</label>
                <div><input type="checkbox" id="setOsLifecycleEnabled">
                    <span id="osLifecycleInfo" class="hint"></span>
                    <div class="hint">Support/end-of-life dates of OS releases are downloaded from the public endoflife.date API with every NVD
                    refresh and cached; nothing about your devices is sent. Off or offline: the support state is "unknown" and no OS-EOL finding is raised.</div></div>

                <label for="setOsLifecycleUrl">Lifecycle API URL</label>
                <div><input type="text" id="setOsLifecycleUrl" style="width:420px">
                    <select id="setOsLifecycleUrlSrc" class="srcsel"></select>
                    <div class="hint">https, ending with "/" (the product slug + ".json" is appended). Only change this for a mirror.</div></div>

                <label for="setOsUrgentDays">OS upgrade is urgent this many days before support ends</label>
                <div><input type="text" id="setOsUrgentDays" class="num">
                    <select id="setOsUrgentDaysSrc" class="srcsel"></select>
                    <div class="hint">OS Updates tab: an outdated release counts as "Upgrade urgent" once its support (endoflife.date)
                    has ended or fewer days than this are left, otherwise as "Upgrade available". 365 = default, 0 = only after support ended.
                    Windows Home/Pro releases get 24 months of support, so with 365 a Pro release becomes urgent about a year after it came out.</div></div>

                <label for="setNotifyOnScan">Notify admins after scans</label>
                <div><input type="checkbox" id="setNotifyOnScan"></div>

                <label for="setNotifyThreshold">Global notify threshold</label>
                <div><select id="setNotifyThreshold">
                        <option value="CRITICAL">Critical and above</option>
                        <option value="HIGH">High and above</option>
                        <option value="MEDIUM">Medium and above</option>
                        <option value="LOW">Low and above</option>
                        <option value="UNKNOWN">Everything</option>
                    </select></div>

                <label for="setNotifyRepeat">Repeat unrated findings every scan</label>
                <div><input type="checkbox" id="setNotifyRepeat">
                    <div class="hint">Notification becomes a to-do list: findings stay listed as "(severity, open)" until they are rated or flagged. New ones are always reported once as "(severity, new)".</div></div>
            </div>

            <h3>Device groups</h3>
            <div class="hint" style="margin-bottom:6px;">"Scan" unchecked for <b>all</b> groups = scan <b>all</b> groups (an empty selection means all).
                A per-group threshold overrides the global one for notifications from that group.</div>
            <div class="hint" style="margin-bottom:10px;"><b>What the notify threshold does:</b> after every scan the
                plugin notifies all site admins about the findings of that run. <em>Global notify threshold</em> (above)
                is the severity floor for all groups - e.g. HIGH means "report findings of severity HIGH and worse".
                The per-group selection in this table <b>overrides that floor for one group only</b>: a group with a
                lot of noise can be set to CRITICAL so it only shouts for the worst findings, while a sensitive group
                can be set to LOW or UNKNOWN so everything is reported. "Global default" means the group follows the
                global floor. The <b>Source</b> column says where the value in the select comes from: <em>set here</em>
                (saved in this plugin's settings), <em>from config.json</em> (the server file) or
                <em>global threshold</em> (no per-group value - the global floor applies).</div>
            <div class="table-container">
                <table>
                    <thead><tr><th>Group</th><th>Scan</th><th>Notify threshold</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead>
                    <tbody id="groupTableBody"><tr><td colspan="4" style="color:#888">Loading...</td></tr></tbody>
                </table>
            </div>

            <div class="controls" style="margin-top:16px;">
                <button id="saveSettingsBtn" data-help="set.save">Save Settings</button>
                <button id="resetSettingsBtn" class="red" data-help="set.reset">Reset all to config.json</button>
            </div>
            <div id="settingsMsg"></div>
        </div>
